    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d103-a2">

                <pb facs="0325" n="241" sameAs="frus:frus1886/pg241"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No. 117.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Goddard to Mr.
                            Reinberg.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Consular, Agency</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Bahia</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1885-04-06"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 6,
                        1885</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 27.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform you that I
                    arrived back here yesterday by the steamer. I find that it will be impossible to
                    obtain the proofs required for the Santos case to send forward by this steamer.
                    I will therefore send them forward by the land post.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>E. T. GODDARD,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">United States Consular
                            Agent.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
